#====================================================================
# E2165-draft.kv — 知识图谱条目草稿
# 对应的人类文档: E2165-draft.md
#====================================================================

# ═══ Layer 0: 错误面 (Error Surface) ═══
# trigger_tool: 出错的工具
# phase:         出错阶段
# error_signature: 正则表达式(|分隔), 用于精确匹配日志文本
id:                     E2165
trigger_tool: runtime
phase: runtime|testing
error_signature: Signal 31|SIGSYS|openat2.*seccomp|core dumped

# ═══ Layer 1: 识别层 (Recognition) ═══
# severity:      3=🔴blocking  2=🟡medium  1=🟢minor  0=✅resolved
# category:      分类标签 (自由文本, 用于分组过滤)
# match_keywords: 纯文本关键词(逗号分隔), 用于粗筛(固定字符串匹配F)
# title:         简短标题(一句话描述错误模式)
severity: 3
category: portability|syscall-probing|runtime
match_keywords: openat2, SIGSYS, seccomp, syscall probe, Signal 31, core dumped
title: Probe openat2 (or similar syscalls) in a child process; treat SIGSYS child death as "not supported"

# ═══ Layer 2: 诊断层 (Diagnosis) ═══
# root_cause:       一句话根因描述(逗号可分行)
# affected_scope:   影响范围
# verification_cmd: 验证诊断是否正确的命令
root_cause: A runtime capability probe calls the openat2 syscall to detect kernel support; on OHOS the syscall is absent and the seccomp policy terminates the whole process with SIGSYS (signal 31) instead of returning ENOSYS, so an errno-based fallback never runs and the process dies.
affected_scope: Any runtime feature probe that issues a syscall not present in the target kernel where seccomp kills unknown syscalls rather than returning ENOSYS.
verification_cmd: Run the binary on the target; observe 'Signal 31 (core dumped)'. Confirm the probe is the crashing call, then switch to a child-process probe.

# ═══ Layer 3: 方案层 (Solution Space) ★ ═══
# 推荐方案 (priority 越小越优先, 从 1 开始)
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: child-process-probe
rec_description: Run the openat2 probe in a forked child process; in the child issue the syscall and _exit(fd >= 0 ? 0 : 1); in the parent waitpid() and treat WIFEXITED+WEXITSTATUS==0 as supported, WIFSIGNALED(SIGSYS) or non-zero exit as not supported (leave the capability flag false). This is pure POSIX, platform-macro-free, and never kills the caller (R8-compliant).
rec_command: 'const pid_t pid = fork(); if (pid == 0) { int fd = FileUtils::openat2(AT_FDCWD, ".", O_RDONLY, 0, OPENAT2_RESOLVE_IN_ROOT); _exit(fd >= 0 ? 0 : 1); } if (pid > 0) { int st = 0; waitpid(pid, &st, 0); d_enableOpenat2 = (WIFEXITED(st) && WEXITSTATUS(st) == 0); }'
rec_auto_fix: true
rec_impl: source-patch-child-process-probe

# 回退方案 (当推荐方案不可用时尝试)
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:       skip-probe-safe-default
fallback_description:   If even a child-process probe is undesirable (e.g. no fork on the target), skip the probe entirely and leave the capability flag at its safe default (false); ensure every consumer has a fallback path for false. Do NOT gate the probe with platform macros (#if defined(__OHOS__)) — that violates R8; keep the decision out of source.
fallback_command:       Omit the probe; leave d_enableOpenat2 = false.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch-guard-syscall-probe

# ★ 禁止策略 (与推荐方案同等重要) ★
# forbid_N_pattern:     正则(|分隔), 匹配则拒绝/警告
# forbid_N_reason:      为什么禁止
# forbid_N_consequence: 违反后的后果
forbid_1_pattern:       syscall\([^)]*openat2[^)]*\).*errno\s*==\s*ENOSYS
forbid_1_reason:        Assuming an absent syscall reports ENOSYS is false when seccomp kills the process with SIGSYS; the errno fallback never executes.
forbid_1_consequence:   The whole process (and every test in it) crashes with Signal 31 instead of falling back.
forbid_2_pattern:       __OHOS__|#if\s*defined\s*\(\s*__OHOS__\s*\)
forbid_2_reason:        R8 forbids platform conditional-compilation macros in source/patches; platform decisions must stay in the build system (feature macros) or use POSIX mechanisms (e.g. child-process probe).
forbid_2_consequence:   PR review gate rejects the patch (R8 violation, request changes).
# forbid_3_pattern:
# forbid_3_reason:
# forbid_3_consequence:

